## Context

When DeepSeek V3.2 receives prompts exceeding ~2x its context window
(163K), it returns tool_calls (web search requests) instead of extracting
from the provided documents. This happens in 16/20 over-context runs.
The 4 exceptions (p2_census, p2_no_narratives, p2_statistics×2) succeed
despite being 1.6-2.3x over context.

Kimi K2 Thinking (131K context window) handles the same over-context
condition gracefully: 6/6 runs at 160K-282K tokens succeed, including
one at 2.2x over context (F1=0.84).

This is a publishable finding about model failure modes under context
pressure — relevant to the article's discussion of model limitations.

## Actions

1. Add a paragraph to report/report.tex in the discussion or limitations
   section noting the over-context behavior difference.
2. Include: context window sizes, token counts, refusal rates, and the
   contrast between DeepSeek (tool_calls escape) and Kimi (graceful
   degradation).
3. Optionally add a small table showing the over-context runs.

## Test

`make report` compiles. The over-context finding is mentioned in the
article text.

## Exit criteria

- Article discusses DeepSeek over-context tool_calls behavior
- Contrast with Kimi's graceful handling documented
- LaTeX builds without errors
